       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and it raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas one of these intended?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day and the usual maximum.\n- **1,700 mg per day**, divided as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm that and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was verified. I'd still recommend checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
