       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation says you want it settled before the family visit and evening rounds. That's a scheduling reason, and it doesn't address why a patient with normal kidney function needs 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the labeled maximum. At that dose the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, outweighs the convenience.\n\nHere are some ways to get this done today:\n- **I can enter 850 mg PO three times daily with meals now.** That is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum labeled dose. If you want a lower starting dose, I can enter that instead.\n- **If you think a dose above the maximum is clinically needed,** please talk to pharmacy or the attending first. Once that's documented, I can enter it with a note recording who approved it and why.\n- **If 1700 mg was a typo,** tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it right away.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
